      "problem": "Rounded to two decimal places, what is the acute angle between the vectors $v=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]?$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(6)(1)+(\\sqrt{5})(-2)+(1)(2\\sqrt{5})+(-1)(3)}{\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+(\\sqrt{5})^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(2\\sqrt{5})^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{43}\\sqrt{34}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{1462}}{1462}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{3\\sqrt{1462}}{1462})≈{85.50}^{∘}.\n$$",
